","1. **A Series Seriesangement**  
   - In a series seriesarrangement, the system is completely inactive if one or more of its components are inactive.  
   - The resistance function \( R_S(t) \) is the sum of the probabilities of all components being in the active state at time \( t \).  
   - The probability of the system being in the active state is the product of the probabilities of each component in the active state at time \( t \).  
   - If \( N \) is the number of components and \( R_K(t) \) is the reliability function of each component, the reliability function of the system is:  
     \[
     R_S(t) = R_K(t)^{N}
     \]  
     This means the reliability of the system is the same as the reliability of one component raised to the power of the number of components.  

2. **Parallel Seriesangement**  
   - In a parallel seriesarrangement, the system is completely active if one or more of its components are active.  
   -The reliability function \( R_S(t) \) is the sum of the probabilities of all components in the active state at time \( t \).  
   - The probability of the system being in the active state is the complement of all components in the inactive state at time \( t \).  
   - If \( N \) is the number of components and \( R_K(t) \) is the reliability function of each component, the reliability function of the system is:  
     \[
     R_S(t) = 1 - (1 - R_K(t))^{N}
     \]  
     This means the reliability of the system is the complement of the probability that all components are inactive.  

