   \]

2. **Determine the speed difference:**  
   The difference in speed is \( 20 \text{ km/h} - 10 \text{ km/h} = 10 \text{ km/h} \).  
   This means B travels 10 km longer than A during the same time.

3. **Determine the time it takes for B to cross A:**  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{ \text{Speed difference}} = \frac{30 \text{ km}}{10 \text{ km/h}} = 3 \text{ hrs}
   \]

4. **Calculate the distance B travels to cross A:**  
   \[
   \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 20 \text{ km/h} \times 3 \text{ hr} = 60 \text{ km}
   \]

