","To find the magnetic field strength at the center of a circular coil, we can use the formula:

B = (μ₀ * N * I) / (2 * π * r)

where B is the magnetic field strength, μ₀ is the permeability of free space (4π × 10^(-7) Tm/A), N is the number of turns, I is the current, and r is the radius of the coil.

Given the values:
N = 100
I = 1 A
r = 0.2 m

Plugging these values into the formula:

B = (4π × 10^(-7) Tm/A * 100 * 1 A) / (2 * π * 0.2 m)

B = (4π × 10^(-7) * 100) / (0.4π)

B = (4 × 10^(-5) * 100) / 0.4

B = 4 × 10^(-3) / 0.4

B = 100 * 10^(-3)

B = 1 × 10^(-2) T

So, the magnetic field strength at the center of the coil is 1 × 10^(-2) T or 0.01 T.",relevance,"# Task Description
