</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The maximum deflection of a timber truss beam is given by:  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{PL^3}{3EI}
\]  
For a truss beam, the moment of inertia \( I = \frac{b t^2}{2} \). Substituting this into the formula:  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{PL^3}{3EI} = \frac{PL^3}{3EI} = \frac{PL^3}{3EI}
\]  
Substituting \( I = \frac{b t^2}{2} \):  
\[
\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{PL^3}{3E\left(\frac{b t^2}{2}\right)} = \frac{2PL^3}{3Eb t^2}
\]  
Thus, the maximum deflection is:  
\[
\boxed{\delta_{\text{max}} = \frac{2PL^3}{3Ebt^2}}
\]
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

