","To compute the curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) in a Cartesian coordinate system, we use the formula:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \begin{vmatrix}
\mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
\frac{\partial}{\partial x} & \frac{\partial}{\partial y} & \frac{\partial}{\partial z} \\
u(x, y, z) & u'(x, y, z) & u''(x, y, z)
\end{vmatrix},
\]
where \(\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{i} u(x, y, z) + \mathbf{j} u'(x, y, z) + \mathbfmathbf{k} u''(x, y, z)\). 

For a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) that depends only on \(x\) and \(y\), we can write \(\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{i} f(x, y) + \mathbf{j} f'(x, y) + \mathbf{0} \mathbf{k}\), where \(f(x, y)\) is a scalar scalar-valued function. 

Substituting this into the curl formula:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \begin{vmatrix}
\mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\

\frac{\partial}{\partial x} & \frac{\partial}{\partial y} & \0 \\
f(x, y) & f'(x, y) & 0
\endendpmatrix.
\]
Expanding the determinant, we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \mathbf{i} \left( \mathbf{j} \cdot 0 - \mathbf{k} \cdot f'(x, y) \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( \mathbf{j} \cdot 0 - \mathbf{k} \cdot f(x, y) \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( \mathbf{i} \cdot f''(x, y) - \mathbf{j} \cdot f'(x, y) \right).
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = -\mathbf{i} f'(x, y) + \mathbf{j} f(x, y).
\]

Thus, the curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) that depends only on \(x\) and \(y\) is:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \mathbf{i} \frac{\partial}{\partial y} f(x, y) - \mathbf{j} \frac{\partial}{\partial x} f(x, y).
\]",fluency,"# Task Description
